asants. Svekolnik is a related cold beet soup in Russian cuisine, commonly made with bread kvass or beetroot kvass."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-cold-beet-soup"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cold_beet_soup"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Belarusian cuisine","cuisine/belarusian-cuisine"],["Latvian cuisine","cuisine/latvian-cuisine"],["Lithuanian cuisine","cuisine/lithuanian-cuisine"],["Polish cuisine","cuisine/polish-cuisine"],["Ukrainian cuisine","cuisine/ukrainian-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":4,"links":[["Beetroot","ingredient/beetroot"],["Kefir","ingredient/kefir"],["Kvass","ingredient/kvass"],["Sorrel","ingredient/sorrel"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Latvian Eats","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"latvianeats.com","note":"English-language blog of traditional Latvian recipes, including a project cooking through old Latvian cookbooks.","url":"https://latvianeats.com","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"},{"name":"Polonist","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"polonist.com","note":"Polish recipes and food culture from a Polish-born writer living abroad.","url":"https://www.polonist.com/about/","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"},{"name":"Polish Your Kitchen","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"polishyourkitchen.com","note":"Long-running blog of traditional Polish home recipes.","url":"https://polishyourkitchen.com","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"},{"name":"Savas Kitchen: Ukrainian recipes","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"savaskitchen.com","note":"Ukrainian-born home cook Nataliia Savas's section of family Ukrainian recipes.","url":"https://savaskitchen.com/category/ukrainian-recipes","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"}]},{"h":"More from Belarusian cuisine","links":[["Angel wings","dish/angel-wings"],["Aspic","dish/aspic"],["Baba (cake)","dish/baba-cake"],["Borscht","dish/borscht"],["Cabbage roll","dish/cabbage-roll"],["Gugelhupf","dish/gugelhupf"],["Kalduny","dish/kalduny"],["Kasha","dish/kasha"],["Krupnik (soup)","dish/krupnik-soup"],["Medovukha","dish/medovukha"],["Mimosa salad","dish/mimosa-salad"],["Paska (bread)","dish/paska-bread"],["Potato pancake","dish/potato-pancake"],["Šakotis","dish/sakotis"],["Salceson","dish/salceson"],["Solyanka","dish/solyanka"],["Sorrel soup","dish/sorrel-soup"],["Syrniki","dish/syrniki"],["Zatiruha","dish/zatiruha"],["Zrazy","dish/zrazy"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/3/37/Lurid_borscht.jpg/500px-Lurid_borscht.jpg","w":500,"h":386,"by":"User:TreasuryTag","lic":"CC BY-SA 3.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Lurid_borscht.jpg"}},"dish/discada":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/discada","n":"Discada","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish found in 2 cuisines","dot":"#94bd5c","intro":[["A discada is a large disc cookware found in Mexican and Southwestern US cooking. It is also the name for a mixed meat dish made with this cooking utensil."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-discada"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Discada"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Southwestern American cuisine","cuisine/cuisine-of-the-southwestern-united-states"],["Mexican cuisine","cuisine/mexican-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Mexico in My Kitchen","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"mexicoinmykitchen.com","note":"Mely Martínez's long-running blog of Mexican home-style recipes.","url":"https://www.mexicoinmykitchen.com/","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"},{"name":"Pati Jinich","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"patijinich.com","note":"Recipe archive from the Mexican-born chef and host of the PBS series Pati's Mexican Table.","url":"https://patijinich.com/recipes/","suggested":true,"kind":"site"}]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/9/9f/DISCADA.JPG/500px-DISCADA.JPG","w":500,"h":380,"by":"Gabriel.ibanez.lito","lic":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:DISCADA.JPG"}},"ingredient/oyster-sauce":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/oyster-sauce","n":"Oyster sauce","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 2 dishes across 3 cuisines","intro":[["Oyster sauce describes a number of sauces made by cooking oysters. The most common in modern use is a viscous dark brown condiment made from oyster extracts, sugar, salt and water, thickened with corn starch (though original oyster sauce reduced the unrefined sugar through heating, resulting in a naturally thick sauce due to caramelization, not the addition of corn starch)."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-oyster-sauce"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Oyster_sauce"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":3,"groups":[["Lao cuisine","cuisine/lao-cuisine",[["Drunken noodles","dish/drunken-noodles"]]],["Thai cuisine","cuisine/thai-cuisine",[["Drunken noodles","dish/drunken-noodles"]]],["Vietnamese cuisine","cuisine/vietnamese-cuisine",[["Shaking beef","dish/shaking-beef"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Fish sauce","ingredient/fish-sauce"],["Peppercorn","ingredient/peppercorn"],["Soy sauce","ingredient/soy-sauce"],["Baby corn","ingredient/baby-corn"],["Bean sprout","ingredient/bean-sprout"],["Chicken","ingredient/chicken"],["Chili pepper","ingredient/chili-pepper"],["Garlic","ingredient/garlic"],["Holy basil","ingredient/holy-basil"],["Pisum sativum subsp. sativum convar. axiphium","ingredient/pisum-sativum-subsp-sativum-convar-axiphium"],["Shahe fen","ingredient/shahe-fen"],["Shrimp","ingredient/shrimp"],["Sugar","ingredient/sugar"],["Tofu","ingredient/tofu"],["Beef","ingredient/beef"],["Bell pepper","ingredient/bell-pepper"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/7/78/OysterSauce2.jpg/500px-OysterSauce2.jpg","w":500,"h":375,"by":"Gossipguy","lic":"CC BY-SA 3.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:OysterSauce2.jpg"}},"dish/khingalsh":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/khingalsh","n":"Khingalsh","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Chechen cuisine","dot":"#f0b340","intro":[["Khingalsh is a traditional Chechen pie filled with pumpkin or sweet potato and served with butter or clarified butter. The pies are typically cut into pieces before serving."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-khingalsh"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Khingalsh"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Chechen cuisine","cuisine/chechen-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":1,"links":[["Pumpkin","ingredient/pumpkin"]]},{"h":"More from Chechen cuisine","links":[["Blini","dish/blini"],["Vieta (dish)","dish/vieta-dish"],["Zhizhig-galnash","dish/zhizhig-galnash"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/c/ca/%D0%A5%D0%B8%D0%BD%D0%B3%D0%B0%D0%BB%D1%88_%28%D1%84%D0%B0%D0%B9%D0%BB_1%29.jpg/500px-%D0%A5%D0%B8%D0%BD%D0%B3%D0%B0%D0%BB%D1%88_%28%D1%84%D0%B0%D0%B9%D0%BB_1%29.jpg","w":500,"h":375,"by":"Дагиров Умар","lic":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%D0%A5%D0%B8%D0%BD%D0%B3%D0%B0%D0%BB%D1%88_(%D1%84%D0%B0%D0%B9%D0%BB_1).jpg"}},"dish/manchow-soup":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/manchow-soup","n":"Manchow soup","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Indian Chinese cuisine","dot":"#f0b340","intro":[["Manchow soup is a popular type of soup exclusive to Indo-Chinese cuisine, due to its easy preparation and hot, spicy taste. It is available in many restaurants and street food carts. Although the soup is named after the Asian region of Manchuria, it does not resemble food that is normally found in the region and is instead from the state of Meghalaya."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-manchow-soup"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Manchow_soup"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Indian Chinese cuisine","cuisine/indian-chinese-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":1,"links":[["Scallion","ingredient/scallion"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/0/02/Manchow_soup_-_Indo-Chinese_cuisine.jpg/500px-Manchow_soup_-_Indo-Chinese_cuisine.jpg","w":500,"h":333,"by":"Sarkar Sayantan","lic":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Manchow_soup_-_Indo-Chinese_cuisine.jpg"}},"ingredient/sauce-bourguignonne":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/sauce-bourguignonne","n":"Sauce Bourguignonne","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 1 dish across 2 cuisines","intro":[["Sauce bourguignonne is a French sauce with a base of red wine with onions or shallots, a bouquet garni (parsley, thyme and bay leaf), reduced, strained, and mixed with some espagnole sauce. Just before serving it is mounted with butter and seasoned lightly with cayenne pepper. Like all red wine sauces, it may have some mushrooms added during cooking to enrich the flavour."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-sauce-bourguignonne"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sauce_bourguignonne"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":2,"groups":[["French cuisine","cuisine/french-cuisine",[["Oeufs en meurette","dish/oeufs-en-meurette"]]],["New Caledonian cuisine","cuisine/new-caledonian-cuisine",[["Oeufs en meurette","dish/oeufs-en-meurette"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Poached egg","ingredient/poached-egg"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/d/d3/Roti_de_boeuf_%C3%A0_la_bourguignonne.jpg/500px-Roti_de_boeuf_%C3%A0_la_bourguignonne.jpg","w":500,"h":367,"by":"Like_the_Grand_Canyon","lic":"CC BY 2.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/2.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Roti_de_boeuf_%C3%A0_la_bourguignonne.jpg"}},"ingredient/cucurbita":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/cucurbita","n":"Cucurbita","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 2 dishes across 4 cuisines","intro":[["Cucurbita (Latin for 'gourd') is a genus, native to the Andes and Mesoamerica, of herbaceous fruits in the gourd family, Cucurbitaceae (also known as cucurbits or cucurbi). Five edible species are grown and consumed for their flesh and seeds. They are variously known as squash, pumpkin, or gourd, depending on species, variety, and local parlance. Other kinds of gourd, also called bottle gourds, are native to Africa and belong to the genus Lagenaria, which is in the same family and subfamily as Cucurbita, but in a different tribe; their young fruits are eaten much like those of the Cucurbita species."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-cucurbita"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cucurbita"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":4,"groups":[["Indonesian cuisine","cuisine/indonesian-cuisine",[["Tinutuan","dish/tinutuan"]]],["Kazakh cuisine","cuisine/kazakh-cuisine",[["Orama (dish)","dish/orama-dish"]]],["Kyrgyz cuisine","cuisine/kyrgyz-cuisine",[["Orama (dish)","dish/orama-dish"]]],["Uzbek cuisine","cuisine/uzbek-cuisine",[["Orama (dish)","dish/orama-dish"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Animal fat","ingredient/animal-fat"],["Brassica","ingredient/brassica"],["Potato","ingredient/potato"],["Pumpkin","ingredient/pumpkin"],["Wheat flour","ingredient/wheat-flour"],["Congee","ingredient/congee"],["Corncob","ingredient/corncob"],["Granulated sugar","ingredient/granulated-sugar"],["Holy basil","ingredient/holy-basil"],["Ipomoea aquatica","ingredient/ipomoea-aquatica"],["Rice","ingredient/rice"],["Salt-cured meat","ingredient/salt-cured-meat"],["Sweet potato","ingredient/sweet-potato"],["Tapioca","ingredient/tapioca"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/e/ea/Squashes_at_Kew_Gardens_IncrEdibles_2013.jpg/500px-Squashes_at_Kew_Gardens_IncrEdibles_2013.jpg","w":500,"h":317,"by":"Chiswick Chap","lic":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Squashes_at_Kew_Gardens_IncrEdibles_2013.jpg"}},"dish/pakistani-rice-dishes":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/pakistani-rice-dishes","n":"Pakistani rice dishes","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Pakistani cuisine","dot":"#f0b340","intro":[["Pakistani rice dishes are popular across the country, and based on Pakistan's role major producer, consumer, and exporter rice, with Basmati being the most commonly used variety. Rice is often served alongside or mixed with other dishes."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-pakistani-rice-dishes"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pakistani_rice_dishes"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Pakistani cuisine","cuisine/pakistani-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Pakistan Eats","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"pakistaneats.substack.com","note":"Maryam Jillani's newsletter on Pakistani food, recipes and food culture.","url":"https://pakistaneats.substack.com/p/pakistani-dishes-for-beginners","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"}]},{"h":"More from Pakistani cuisine","links":[["Bannu pulao","dish/bannu-pulao"],["Falooda","dish/falooda"],["Paratha roll","dish/paratha-roll"],["Reshmi kabab","dish/reshmi-kabab"],["Tandoori roti","dish/tandoori-roti"],["Thali","dish/thali"],["Zarda (food)","dish/zarda-food"]]}]},"dish/rumford-s-soup":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/rumford-s-soup","n":"Rumford's Soup","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Bavarian cuisine","dot":"#cf5f87","intro":[["Rumford's Soup (Rumfordsche Suppe, also called economy soup) was an early effort in scientific nutrition. It was invented by Benjamin Thompson, Reichsgraf von Rumford, circa 1800 and consumed in Munich and greater Bavaria, where he was employed as an advisor to Charles Theodore, Elector of Bavaria. It was used as a ration for the poor, for Bavarian workhouses and military workhouses, and prisoners. Count Rumford has been credited in many instances for \"establishing the first real soup kitchen.\""]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-rumford-s-soup"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rumford's_Soup"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Bavarian cuisine","cuisine/bavarian-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":5,"links":[["Beer","ingredient/beer"],["Pea","ingredient/pea"],["Pearl barley","ingredient/pearl-barley"],["Potato","ingredient/potato"],["Sour beer","ingredient/sour-beer"]]},{"h":"More from Bavarian cuisine","links":[["Bayrisch Kraut","dish/bayrisch-kraut"],["Leberkäse","dish/leberkase"],["Weißwurst","dish/wei-wurst"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/a/ab/Rumfordsuppe.jpg/500px-Rumfordsuppe.jpg","w":500,"h":465,"by":"Gestumblindi","lic":"CC0","licUrl":"http://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/deed.en","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Rumfordsuppe.jpg"}},"dish/selat-solo":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/selat-solo","n":"Selat solo","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Indonesian cuisine","dot":"#f0b340","intro":[["Selat solo is a Javanese dish influenced by Western cuisine; it is a specialty of Solo city, Central Java, Indonesia. It consists of braised beef tenderloin served in thin watery sauce made from a mixture of garlic, vinegar, kecap manis (sweet soy sauce), Worcestershire sauce, water, and spiced with nutmeg and black pepper. It is served with hard boiled egg and vegetables such as string beans, potato, tomato, lettuce, cucumber, cauliflower or broccoli and carrot, and topped with potato chips and some dash of mustard, hollandaise or sauce gribiche on the side."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-selat-solo"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Selat_solo"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Indonesian cuisine","cuisine/indonesian-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":12,"links":[["Beef","ingredient/beef"],["Beef tenderloin","ingredient/beef-tenderloin"],["Carrot","ingredient/carrot"],["Egg","ingredient/egg"],["Green bean","ingredient/green-bean"],["Lettuce","ingredient/lettuce"],["Mayonnaise","ingredient/mayonnaise"],["Onion","ingredient/onion"],["Potato","ingredient/potato"],["Soy sauce","ingredient/soy-sauce"],["Sweet soy sauce","ingredient/sweet-soy-sauce"],["Vinegar","ingredient/vinegar"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Daily Cooking Quest","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"dailycookingquest.com","note":"Indonesian home cook Anita's blog with a large archive of Indonesian recipes.","url":"https://dailycookingquest.com/cuisines/indonesian.html","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"}]},{"h":"More from Indonesian cuisine","links":[["Arem-arem","dish/arem-arem"],["Arsik","dish/arsik"],["Asam pedas","dish/asam-pedas"],["Ayam goreng","dish/ayam-goreng"],["Ayam goreng kalasan","dish/ayam-goreng-kalasan"],["Ayam panggang","dish/ayam-panggang"],["Ayam Taliwang","dish/ayam-taliwang"],["Bajigur","dish/bajigur"],["Bakakak hayam","dish/bakakak-hayam"],["Bakpia","dish/bakpia"],["Bakwan","dish/bakwan"],["Bekasang","dish/bekasang"],["Betutu","dish/betutu"],["Bika ambon","dish/bika-ambon"],["Binte biluhuta","dish/binte-biluhuta"],["Bir pletok","dish/bir-pletok"],["Bolu kukus","dish/bolu-kukus"],["Botok","dish/botok"],["Brem","dish/brem"],["Bubur kacang hijau","dish/bubur-kacang-hijau"],["Bubur ketan hitam","dish/bubur-ketan-hitam"],["Bubur pedas","dish/bubur-pedas"],["Buntil","dish/buntil"],["Burgo (food)","dish/burgo-food"],["Cendol","dish/cendol"],["Cenil","dish/cenil"],["Cilok","dish/cilok"],["Cimpa","dish/cimpa"],["Corn fritter","dish/corn-fritter"],["Coto makassar","dish/coto-makassar"],["Dadar gulung","dish/dadar-gulung"],["Dadiah","dish/dadiah"],["Dengke mas naniura","dish/dengke-mas-naniura"],["Empal gentong","dish/empal-gentong"],["Emping","dish/emping"],["Es buah","dish/es-buah"],["Es doger","dish/es-doger"],["Es goyobod","dish/es-goyobod"],["Gado-gado","dish/gado-gado"],["Geplak","dish/geplak"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/3/36/Selat_Solo.jpg/500px-Selat_Solo.jpg","w":500,"h":386,"by":"Gunawan Kartapranata","lic":"CC BY-SA 3.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Selat_Solo.jpg"}}}